# Copy to .env.local for development. .env* is gitignored except this example.
#
# Skiron has no backend. The key is sent from the browser straight to Google and
# is never written to a file, a URL, a log, a save or an exported case
# (invariant 9). This file exists so a developer does not have to paste the key
# into the settings screen on every reload; a player uses the settings screen.
#
# Vite inlines anything prefixed VITE_ into the client bundle at build time, so
# DO NOT set this in a production build — the key would ship to every visitor.
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# The Node-side authoring CLI (`npm run author`) does not read this file. It
# takes --key=..., then $GEMINI_API_KEY, then %USERPROFILE%\Desktop\gkey.txt,
# read at call time, as catalog-art does.
